# Cliffhanger resolvers. They live in their own file, sorted ahead of every other
# deck file, so a resolver is the first callback of its day. Hooks: 70_hooks.lv.

card r_band
type event
cat grim
due
once
days 31 35
roles A
when fired h_band
when is A hook_who
text It came back six knocks late and still on the beat. {A} lays the gap on the temperature maps: the night side's coldest hour. Each cold night the gap is a knock or two longer. {A} runs the line forward. It runs past entry week, to a week or two after landing.
do morale A -2

card r_pressure
type event
cat repair
due
once
days 5 36
roles A
when fired h_pressure
when is A hook_who
text {A} spent four hours panel by panel with a leak detector, suit staged at the hatch. The culprit was a cable feedthrough whose seal shrank in the shaded-side cold. The trend goes in the logbook like a fish someone caught; under it, the reserve line, which won't recover before Mars.
do res spares -1
do morale A 5

card r_flare
type event
cat grim
due
once
days 8 34
roles A
when fired h_flare
when is A hook_who
text Seven crews spent the night in their shelters between the water tanks, listening to the dosimeters tick. By morning: a month's dose in six hours. {A} wrote down the peak and slept till noon. The dose model now gives each of them a number for later, in a column headed "lifetime".
do var storms 1
do morale A 3

card r_thruster
type event
cat repair skill
due
once
days 5 36
roles A
when fired h_thruster
when is A hook_who
lean brave manual watch
text The ship was steady again within a quarter of an hour.
option manual | Hand control | {A} took attitude into manual and held it while the valve telemetry scrolled past. One valve reported "closed" while it leaked. It's isolated now, and that axis flies one thruster short for the rest of the voyage.
  trait A brave 2
  morale A 4
  set valve_out
  who valve_who A
  mark t_valve
  res fuel -1
option watch | Isolate and watch | {A} let the control loop fight it and watched the pulses, counting. Every one traced to a single valve that reported "closed" while it leaked. It's isolated now, and that axis flies one thruster short for the rest of the voyage.
  trait A curious 2
  morale A 4
  set valve_out
  who valve_who A
  mark t_valve
  res fuel -1

card r_flood
type event
cat repair skill
due
once
days 5 36
roles A
when fired h_flood
when is A hook_who
text The night's record: {A} found it buried on page nine, a coolant pump drawing too much current, minutes from tripping. {A} swapped to the backup before the primary died. By morning the alarm list was down from 214 to a page. The backup is the only pump now.
do morale A 5
do res spares -1

card r_silence
type event
cat grim
due
once
days 11 36
roles A
when fired h_silence
when is A hook_who
text The reply arrived before breakfast. A ground station had gone down in a storm at home, and the backup had to wait for Earth to turn. For eight hours the fleet was on its own, and the checklist for that is one page long. The message ends: "All good here. How are you?" {A} starts with the weather.
do morale A 6
do trait A warm 2

card r_strike
type event
cat grim
due
once
days 5 36
roles A B
when fired h_strike
when is A hook_who
when cond B ok
when !is B eva_who
when home A
when !is A eva_who
text {A}'s morning EVA, {B} suited at the next ship's hatch, found a fingernail crater in a heat-shield tile, short of the bondline. The entry team clears it on one condition: {A}'s ship flies entry a few tenths of a degree steeper, for a sharper peak and a shorter soak.
do trait A brave 2
do morale A 3

card r_ghost
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 26 34
roles A
when fired h_ghost
when is A hook_who
text {A} pinned it down by morning: a launch cover plate shed at departure, on almost the fleet's own orbit, turning end over end and gaining about fifteen metres an hour. Tonight it slides past forty kilometres off the bow. {A} writes it up, and Starbase starts counting its cover plates.
do trait A curious 3
do morale A -2

card r_voice
type event
cat human
due
once
days 26 34
roles A
when fired h_voice
when is A hook_who
text {A} traced it the next morning: a message from home, recorded the night before launch and queued for this flight day. Last week's intercom update reset its clock, so it fired in the night and cut out when the buffer ran dry. The rest plays at breakfast. {A} listens with the volume very low.
do morale A 6
do trait A warm 3

card r_dark
type event
cat grim
due
once
days 27 32
roles A
when fired h_dark
when is A hook_who
when !flag signal_answered
text {A} was back inside three hours. An old-channel frame, a link request with a field the new stack had never seen, hung the comms computer, then the backup; the third boot quarantined it. The ground takes the old channel off the fleet net. The listening dish keeps recording.
do trait A brave 3
do morale A -2

card r_dark_a
type event
cat grim
due
once
days 27 32
roles A
when fired h_dark
when is A hook_who
when flag signal_answered
text {A} was back inside three hours. An old-channel frame, a link request with a field the new stack had never seen, hung the comms computer, then the backup; the third boot quarantined it. The ground moves the channel to a sandbox; the hellos go on from a box that can't hang a radio.
do trait A brave 3
do morale A -2

